We then create a DomainBuilder to define the HTN domain, which consists of a tree of selectors and sequences. Each node in the tree represents a task that the planner can perform, and its conditions and effects on the world state. We use the DomainBuilder to construct a domain by chaining together the appropriate methods.

To generate a plan, we instantiate a Planner and a Context, initialize the Context, and repeatedly call the planner's Tick method with the domain and context until the desired goal is achieved. In this example, the goal is to set the "Done" flag in the context to true. When the goal is achieved, we should see the console output "Get A", "Get B", "Get C", and "Done".
