1. Initialize the number of people n and the gap k between the executed individuals.
2. Create an array of size n and fill it with numbers from 1 to n.
3. Initialize a counter i to 0.
4. While there is more than one person remaining in the array, repeat steps 5-6:
5. Increment i by k.
6. Remove the person at index (i mod n) from the array.
7. Return the last remaining person in the array.

