```
let switchCheckbox = document.getElementById("switch");
let switchContainer = document.querySelector(".switch-container");

switchCheckbox.addEventListener("click", function(){
  switchContainer.classList.toggle("night-mode");
});
```

This will toggle the "night-mode" class on the switch container when the checkbox is clicked. You can also add some styles to this class to change the appearance of the page in night mode. To enable text selection behind the switch, you can set `pointer-events: none` on the label element in CSS:

```
.switch-container label {
  pointer-events: none;
}
```

This will allow mouse events to pass through the label element, so you can still select text behind it. When the night mode is enabled, you can set `pointer-events: all` to make the switch clickable again.

